That's so incredible!

164
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:20,500
Five, four, three, two, one!

165
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,160
Now begin!

166
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:27,380
Two, three, four, five, six, ready, pose!

167
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:29,880
Why are you a pretzel?

168
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:31,340
I can do it perfectly in my head,

169
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,060
but my body is not quite there yet.

170
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:34,200
Look, Sakura!

171
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,440
She's gonna break her neck and end up like us!

172
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,900
I'm not positive Mai Mai can handle this.

173
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:41,800
Let's try again.

174
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:42,740
Bowie!

175
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:44,200
And fight!

176
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,000
It's not broken!

177
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,100
One more time.

178
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:47,380
And again!

179
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:47,720
No!

180
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:48,840
Again?

181
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:49,580
Hail!

182
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:51,540
That's enough.

183
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:52,740
Let's call it a day for now.

184
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,540
I don't want to stop.

185
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:55,860
I want to be a real member of Fron Shushu

186
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:56,820
as soon as possible!

187
00:07:56,820 --> 00:08:04,320
Make sure to practice what we did today, okay?

188
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:05,400
Right-o!

189
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:06,380
I'll see you tomorrow.

190
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:09,020
Dude.

191
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,980
You're kidding me!

192
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:13,240
It's in color!

193
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:13,840
Sakura!

194
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:14,400
Look!

195
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:15,320
This thing's in color!

196
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:16,880
Oh yeah, that is cool!

197
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,380
Does it have Oya Jichi?

198
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:19,880
Yeah, he's there.

199
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:21,700
It's the 20th anniversary edition!

200
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:23,900
Wicked!

201
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:25,520
I'd be pissed if he wasn't!

202
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:26,680
Love that guy.

203
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,060
You worked really hard today.

204
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,500
I've got a lot to learn.

205
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:34,060
You impressed Ai with the energy you brought.

206
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,360
I just want everyone to accept me.

207
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:39,840
So how long have you been a Fron Shushu superfan?

208
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:43,500
Well, I was beginning to give up on Saga.

209
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:44,580
Huh?

210
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:47,840
And then I realized, this place has a lot of potential.

211
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,800
But nobody knows that.

212
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:53,240
Guess that's just part of Saga's thing, I figure.

213
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:58,400
Like if Saga were Fukuoka, everyone would think of it as a lively place with active residents,

214
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:01,400
and then people would probably care about it a whole lot more.

215
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,360
Yeah, Saga is kind of its own thing.

216
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:06,380
Anyway, one day I was flipping through Saga's zine,

217
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:07,560
and I was like,

218
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:08,180
Whoa!

219
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:09,720
Idols in Saga?

220
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:14,100
I saw that you were doing a show at the end of the year.

221
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:40,200
You liked it that much?

222
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:41,940
It was totally mind-blowing!

223
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:43,700
Oh gosh, thank you.

224
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:45,420
I don't know how to say it,

225
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,980
but I'm amazed at your expression whenever you sing.

226
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:50,140
The way you're able to shine so brightly.

227
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:53,880
It got me thinking more and more about how I wanted to be just like you

228
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:55,420
and live a super cool life in Saga,

229
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:56,960
the same way you and your friends do.

230
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:03,120
You are just like me.

231
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,260
But the EFS show was a real mess.

232
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:08,320
Trust me, we felt it in the crowd, too.

233
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:14,300
I have never wished that I could make my voice ring out louder than I did that day watching my faves up on that stage.

234
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:20,140
But when you played Saga Arena,

235
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:23,140
I realized how amazing you guys truly are!

236
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,380
You may be zombies,

237
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,460
but you're just as alive as anyone!

238
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:32,260
So I don't think you need to worry too much about makeup and superficial stuff like that.

239
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:35,920
Because being able to perform the way you do is loads more special!

240
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:39,280
I know that I can't contribute much yet,

241
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:43,300
but I am willing to do whatever I can for Fron Shushu!

242
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,680
We'll work hard together.

243
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:48,620
Yeah!

244
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:50,420
We're pathetic!

245
00:10:51,140 --> 00:10:54,140
We put all our heads together and this is the best we can do?

246
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:57,220
Let's just go with the beauty pageant again and be done with it.

247
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,600
But that's a cop-out!

248
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:00,720
Not that any of these plans are better!

249
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:03,140
Can't we ink out one decent idea?

250
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:08,640
A school festival show?

251
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,100
If we get popular with high school students,

252
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:12,720
it'll really help with visibility!

253
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,380
The grounds will be so crazy!

254
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:15,380
Trust me!

255
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:16,000
Yeah!

256
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:16,980
Shushu!

257
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,040
Yeah!

258
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:18,780
Shushu!

259
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:19,400
See?

260
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:20,340
Yeah!

261
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,400
Shushu!

262
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:23,220
High schoolers, huh?

263
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:24,600
So look fun!

264
00:11:24,780 --> 00:11:26,720
A worthwhile endeavor, I would say.

265
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:28,280
What do you think?

266
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:34,240
Wipe that stupid smile off, or I will!

267
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:36,400
The crowd you girls tend to attract

268
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:38,740
is a hodgepodge of losers and freaks.

269
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,520
Let's take aim at the demographic

270
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:42,040
that'll shape Saga's future.

271
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:43,600
Kay, what about Mai Mai?

272
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:46,260
She can't get through a routine without hurting herself.

273
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,020
Then get it together quick,

274
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,560
cause she's the star.

275
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:53,660
This concert marks the rebirth of Fron Shushu

276
00:11:53,660 --> 00:11:54,600
as a group of eight,

277
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,320
and the debut of number seven!

278
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:59,240
Do you think you're ready for this?

279
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:02,480
As long as my body doesn't betray me, yes?

280
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:04,700
Then all you gotta do is practice your butt off

281
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:05,420
until the show.

282
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:07,580
Now, let me see your game face!

283
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:08,180
Okay!

284
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:09,780
Come on, mind and body,

285
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:11,360
please be in sync for once!

286
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:14,520
The new Fron Shushu is gonna rock all their socks off!

287
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:15,100
Yeah!

288
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:38,360
Great!

289
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:39,140
You've got it!

290
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:39,960
Awesome!

291
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:43,220
I see you've managed to remain upright this time.

292
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,620
Two days till the show.

293
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:45,900
That was close!

294
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:48,980
Thanks for supporting me!

295
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:50,300
Hey!

296
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:51,920
This calls for a group outing!

297
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:53,740
Let's hit the public bath!

298
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:56,500
It's kinda my thing.

299
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:57,980
I know some great spots...

300
00:12:57,980 --> 00:12:59,080
I hate to say it, Mai Mai,

301
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:01,040
but we're gonna have to pass on that one.

302
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:01,760
Uh-uh.

303
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:03,740
Not that we don't like baths.

304
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:05,600
But they're kinda a dead giveaway.

305
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,520
Oh my gosh!

306
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:08,260
I'm so sorry!

307
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:08,700
I forgot!

308
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:09,920
It's fine!

309
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,480
Actually, it might be fun to go

310
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:12,840
and check out your school instead!

311
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:13,780
Nice!

312
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:15,540
That way we can take over their turf!

313
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:15,840
Whoa!

314
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:19,880
I don't have a lot of memories from high school, actually.

315
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:21,220
Yeah, neither do I.

316
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:23,700
I'd be interested to see how the young people of today

317
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:24,580
spin their youth.

318
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:25,320
Great!

319
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:26,260
Let's do it!

320
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:28,000
I can get permission from my teacher!

321
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:28,940
Oh, boy!

322
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:31,520
Hurry up!

323
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:32,680
The festival's tomorrow!

324
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,300
That was such a drag, right?

325
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:39,540
I'm sorry.

326
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,280
The others kind of took off.

327
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:42,320
No worries!

328
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:44,640
Everyone's pumped about the cultural festival tomorrow,

329
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,360
so they are sure to run into excited students wherever they go.

330
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,280
You're right.

331
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,920
The prep always was half the fun.

332
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,760
So, what were you like in your high school days, Sakura?

333
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:54,820
Hmm.

334
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:57,220
Kinda dead on the inside.

335
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,120
Well, you see, some disappointing stuff happened.

336
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:04,340
So I had trouble taking anything seriously.

337
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:07,080
Are you saying that you'd lost all hope?

338
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:07,480
Mm-hmm.

339
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,900
But then I saw Iron Frill.

340
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:13,020
And I was so inspired by I and the rest of the group

341
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:15,240
that I built up the strength to keep moving forward.

342
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:18,920
Around that time, you could always find me practicing

343
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,300
in a corner of the classroom.

344
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:22,540
So I was super happy when I found out

345
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:23,980
they were auditioning new members.

346
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:28,740
But then I died before I got to apply.

347
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,660
Being a zombie isn't all bad, though,

348
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:33,700
because now I get another chance.

349
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:35,460
After meeting the rest of the group,

350
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:37,620
I feel like I can take on any challenge,

351
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,980
even an EFS do-over show.

352
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:41,480
Huh?

353
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,720
Huh? Wait, what?

354
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,920
You're going back?

355
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:46,340
Nobody told you that?

356
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:47,440
Definitely not.

357
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:50,060
That was a catastrophe for you, remember?

358
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,780
Why would you want to do that to yourself again?

359
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:56,340
That's who Fran Shushu is.

360
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,760
Look, I know.

361
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:00,740
EFS was a total mistake.

362
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:01,900
We ended up in debt,

363
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:03,440
and we couldn't even do idle stuff

364
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:04,840
for a pretty long time.

365
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:06,020
But still,

366
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:07,260
none of us gave up.

367
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:09,500
Sure, it's scary to think

368
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:10,940
something like that could happen again,

369
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:11,780
but if we're together,

370
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:12,820
we can face anything.

371
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:13,900
And I mean,

372
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,440
if we ever gave up trying,

373
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,240
that'd be worse.

374
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,600
We'd be wandering lost

375
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:19,700
with the rest of the dead.

376
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:23,400
our hearts may not beat anymore,

377
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:24,760
but we're still living

378
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:27,040
because we refuse to quit chasing our dreams.

379
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,080
We keep rising from the ashes.

380
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:33,640
Oh my gosh, I'm so sorry!

381
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:34,760
They came out really corny

382
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:36,080
and kind of conceited, huh?

383
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:38,820
What's the matter?

384
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,320
So that's who Fran Shushu is.

385
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,220
Yeah, and now that we have you

386
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:44,180
as a part of the group,

387
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,580
we're even stronger.

388
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:47,340
Let's make sure that we put on

389
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:48,840
an amazing show tomorrow, okay?

390
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,480
That's who Fran Shushu's number one is.

391
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:56,300
Hey, are you okay there, Mai Mai?

392
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,000
I think maybe you missed the point

393
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,100
